    "description": "Natural Amethyst Crystal Cluster\nDeep Purple Geode Fragment\nNatural Mineral Specimen, 3.47 Pounds\nThis substantial amethyst crystal cluster features a dense concentration of terminated quartz points in varying shades of deep purple. A classic geological specimen, amethyst is prized by collectors for its vibrant coloration and unique crystalline formations, often used as a centerpiece for home decor or within mineral collections for its aesthetic and geological interest.\nNumerous natural crystal terminations with characteristic hexagonal faceting\nDeep purple saturation with translucent to semi-opaque clarity across the points\nNatural rocky matrix base providing a stable foundation for upright display\nSubstantial size with a verified weight of 3.47 pounds\nCondition:\nNatural specimen with primary crystalline structures intact. No large-scale shearing or significant damage to the main cluster terminations. The underside displays the raw, unpolished host rock matrix typical of geode extractions. Natural mineral inclusions and slight surface dust consistent with storage are present.\nAll items are sold as-is. Condition, completeness, and functionality may vary. Items may not be fully tested, authenticated, sorted, or inventoried unless explicitly stated in the listing. For bulk, lot, or miscellaneous listings, contents can include a mix of brands, types, and conditions, and there are no guarantees regarding specific items included.\nAutographs and signatures have not been authenticated unless otherwise noted.\nWatches and electronics may not be tested for full functionality and may only be tested for power on, if at all.\nDue to the nature of these items, no returns or refunds will be accepted for condition, completeness, or functionality. Buyers are responsible for reviewing all photos and descriptions and must address any questions or concerns prior to bidding or purchase. By placing a bid or completing a purchase, you agree to these terms.\